            <ArticleTitle>Acrodysostosis associated with spinal canal stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1922-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An adult case of acrodysostosis with striking lumbar spinal canal stenosis is reported. She complained of numbness on the right arm, intermittent claudication with numbness on both legs and pain and weakness on the left leg. Although the reduced lumbar interpedicular distance has been reported, no adult case with neurologic symptoms has been reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
